  "narration": "Korin leans back against the rusted railing, one hand resting on a tarnished oar. His eyes narrow slightly, not with anger, but with the weight of years spent watching wanderers come and go.",
  "npc_response": "Friendship isn't a number you can raise on a promise, stranger. I've seen plenty of wanderers claim kinship and then vanish. Trust is earned one crossing at a time. But I'll keep my word about the lantern — if you ever need a ferry, I'll be waiting."
}

{
  "world_updates": [
    {
      "type": "NPC_SPOKE"
    }
  ],
  "memory_summary": "The player asked the Fishermen about strange occurrences, prompting a wary, practical reply tied to his known debt.",
