  "narration": "The Fishermen wipes salt from his brow and leans against the railing, watching the boats come and go. His voice carries the weight of years spent on this pier.",
  "npc_response": "This place? It's been here longer than most of the men who fish from it. Before the boats were even real, it was just a shed where the harbour boys kept their nets and their ale. Now it's where the tide decides who's going out and who's staying in. I've watched a hundred men come through this door, some of them never seen again. The terminal doesn't care who you are — it just holds you until the sea calls. That's all it's ever been for."
